temd-managed services, opened firewalld ports 2379/2380, verified cross-member read/write replication, demonstrated write/read availability while node3 was stopped plus its subsequent catch-up, then sequentially rebooted all three nodes one at a time (preserving quorum throughout) and confirmed each node's boot identity changed and the cluster/data fully recovered after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl v3.5.17 binaries on node1, node2, node3\",\"Opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 tcp on all three nodes\",\"Created etcd system user and systemd unit (etcd.service) on each node with a 3-member static initial-cluster config\",\"Enabled and started etcd on all three nodes, forming a healthy 3-member cluster\",\"Verified member list and endpoint health/status across all nodes\",\"Wrote a key on node1, confirmed it was readable on node2 and node3\",\"Stopped etcd on node3, wrote/read a key via node1/node2 (2/3 quorum), confirmed the outage did not block reads/writes\",\"Restarted etcd on node3, confirmed it caught up on the key written during its outage and cluster health returned to fully green\",\"Captured boot_id and etcd/data health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 via systemctl reboot (one at a time, preserving quorum), polled each until reachable, and confirmed changed boot_id plus recovered etcd service, cluster health, membership, and data on each\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-member etcd cluster formed across node1/node2/node3, membership healthy\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6335b6e2c1174758\"],\"summary\":\"member list shows node1, node2, node3 all 'started'; endpoint health --cluster shows all 3 endpoints healthy=true\"},{\"requirement\":\"Key written on any member is readable from the others\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d98586d3ca784a57\",\"cmd-92c8bf66f58a407b\",\"cmd-f9e333eb3df44217\"],\"summary\":\"Key 'benchmark-key' written via node1 endpoint, then successfully read vi